  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Hurricane Melissa-Affected Communities in Jamaica through Provision of Emergency Shelter, Relief Items, and Displacement Tracking (DTM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project supports communities in Jamaica affected by Hurricane Melissa by strengthening humanitarian response capacity and improving access to timely, life-saving assistance. The hurricane caused damage to homes, disrupted basic services, and increased vulnerabilities among affected households, particularly women, children, older persons, and persons with disabilities. Addressing urgent shelter needs while improving coordination and information remains essential to reduce risks and support recovery.The project combines rapid assessments with the delivery of emergency shelter support and essential relief items. The International Organization for Migration will collect and analyze data on displacement, shelter conditions, and priority needs to inform response planning and coordination with national authorities and humanitarian partners. At the same time, the project will provide emergency shelter materials and essential non-food items to households in the most affected areas, improving safety, dignity, and living conditions.</narrative>
  </description>
